                <pb facs="0969" n="957" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg957"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.35E1A/105: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-02T18:00:00-05:00">October 2, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>407. Your 619, September 28, 6 p.m. There is no objection to inclusion of an
                    Agenda item concerning American Sugar Act for the stated purposes.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
